             finish, per the user's 10-point detail brief:
               - lower-right rebuilt: the title band keeps its approved
                 position with clean air around it; the NEXT item is
                 repositioned VISUALLY (redesigned foreground shard at
                 900,795 380x165, below the title band) so it enters from
                 the bottom edge, partially cropped - a distinct visual
                 space from the title. No placeholder rects anywhere.
               - hero: unchanged treatment (scale, crisp edges, detached
                 contact shadow, restrained blue atmosphere, ONE thin
                 selective yellow rim arc). No concentric decoration.
               - marquee zone substantially larger (24,44 424x252, +31%
                 area): open whitespace, no blue rectangle, no fade; NOW
                 SHOWING stays a tiny kicker.
               - left column: no boxes back. Restrained craftsmanship only:
                 tiny halftone transitions, ONE subtle blueprint fragment,
                 ONE clipped blue geometric intrusion, sparse yellow
                 micro-accents; ~85% stays clean white.
               - typography spacing pass: more air between description and
                 facts, labels quieter, PLAYERS/DEVELOPER baselines
                 standardised, rating with the release-year row.
               - screenshot: ONE clean hairline frame + subtle depth
                 shadow + ONE tiny yellow corner accent. No nested frames.
               - spine: tonal variation within the royal blue, controlled
                 grid texture, ONE continuous thin yellow structural line,
                 supplied logos deliberately MOUNTED on a mounting plate.
               - prev/next: real media, smaller, dimmer, edge-cropped and
                 shard-cropped - a real navigation path, hero dominant.
               - overlap: marquee breaks over its rule, disc overlaps the
                 hero plane, shards crop the neighbours, spine ticks reach
                 into adjacent surfaces.
               - footer quieter still (0.0135, 80FFFFFF).
             Verified against ES-DE 3.4.1: vertical carousel pitch =
             element height / maxItemCount = 1260/3 = 420px; scissor clips
             the partially off-screen neighbours. Motion: native eased
             carousel transitions only - ES-DE has no theme keyframes or
             idle animation, so none is claimed. -->

